# Ziggurat NFL stat vintage capture — TUESDAY timer (item 4.2b).
#
# 08:00 local, TUESDAY only. Two things fix that hour and that day:
#
#   1. TUESDAY IS THE DECISION DAY. `ziggurat waivers` runs Tuesday, the claims
#      are queued Tuesday before ~23:59 PT, and from Week 1 that decision reads
#      whichever stat vintage is newest at the time. This unit is what makes the
#      vintage the decision READ a stored fact instead of a reconstruction.
#   2. AHEAD OF THE 08:20 WEEKLY GROUP, deliberately. The group then finds
#      weekly_stats and snap_counts fresh and pulls only team_defense / ngs_*.
#      That is why this timer carries NO RandomizedDelaySec: the siblings randomise
#      by up to 30 minutes to spread load, and a 30-minute jitter here would let
#      this unit land AFTER the group, at which point the group takes the vintage
#      and this unit's forced pull is a duplicate under the same day stamp — the
#      ordering, not the load spreading, is what this unit is for. One box runs
#      the cadence, so there is nothing to spread.
#
# Persistent=true, and what a catch-up means here: a run that fires late is
# stamped with the day it ACTUALLY ran (retrieved_as_of = the pull day; nothing
# is ever back-stamped), so a Tuesday catch-up that lands on Wednesday is a
# Wednesday vintage and the pair for that week is incomplete. The diff report
# refuses to compare an incomplete pair rather than mislabelling one — the
# refusal is the alarm. A catch-up landing on the same day as the Thursday
# sibling simply re-writes that day's partition with the same file; nothing is
# lost, because a re-pull collides with nothing (retrieved_as_of is in the PK).

[Unit]
Description=Ziggurat NFL stat vintage capture schedule (Tuesday, pre-correction copy)
Documentation=file://@REPO@/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Tue *-*-* 08:00:00
Persistent=true
AccuracySec=1m
Unit=ziggurat-nfl-ingest-vintage-tue.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
